---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use &amp; Disclaimer | Dunhuang &amp; Jiuquan Guide"
  description="Terms of use for the Dunhuang & Jiuquan Guide website: content accuracy, acceptable use, copyright, pricing disclaimers, and liability limits for travelers."
>
  <article class="py-12 md:py-20">
    <div class="u-prose-wrap">
      <header class="mb-16 reveal">
        <SectionHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of Use" subtitle="Last updated: September 8, 2026" />
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-stone max-w-none">
        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing dunhuang-jiuquan.com you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site. We may update these terms; the "last updated" date above reflects the current version.</p>
        <h2>2. Content Accuracy &amp; Pricing Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>We verify ticket prices, transport fares, and opening details in person and against official sources, most recently in July 2026. However, prices, schedules, and policies in China change without notice. Always confirm current prices and booking rules with official channels such as the Dunhuang Academy, attraction ticket offices, or China Railway 12306 before you travel. We are not affiliated with any attraction, hotel, or transport operator.</p>
        <h2>3. Travel Decisions Are Yours</h2>
        <p>This guide is general information, not travel, legal, visa, or safety advice for your specific situation. You are responsible for your own travel decisions, visas, insurance, and compliance with local laws and regulations.</p>
        <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You may not scrape, republish, or resell substantial parts of this site's content without written permission. Personal, non-commercial reference use is welcome, including quoting short passages with a visible link back to the source page.</p>
        <h2>5. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>Original text, photography, route maps, and itineraries on this site are &copy; Dunhuang &amp; Jiuquan Guide. Third-party trademarks and official sources referenced or cited remain the property of their owners.</p>
        <h2>6. External Links</h2>
        <p>We link to official and institutional sources such as UNESCO, the Dunhuang Academy, and China Railway 12306 for verification. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content or availability.</p>
        <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>The site is provided "as is" without warranties. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for losses, costs, or damages arising from use of this site or reliance on its content, including changes in prices, schedules, closures, or travel disruptions.</p>
        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these terms: email <a href="mailto:hello@dunhuang-jiuquan.com" class="text-mogao-600">hello@dunhuang-jiuquan.com</a> or use our <a href="/contact/" class="text-mogao-600">contact page</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy/" class="text-mogao-600">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
